  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1257 AM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nUnimpressive convection continues to fire on the cool side of \nthe +12C isotherm at 700 mb from north central MN into central \nWI. So far there have been no signs of deeper convection \ndeveloping that has a chance to form into an organized complex,\nbut that still may happen overnight. Should that happen, WoFS \nhas been indicating perhaps Rusk County being clipped with that \nactivity. However, given the 700 mb temps and the K-Index \nbecoming less impressive with time across WI, odds are activity \nwill remain east of even Rusk County. A cold front will pass \nthrough this morning and winds will shift northwest and gust \nthis afternoon. Dry air advection will send currently very \nimpressive dew points in the upper 70s to lower 80s down into \nthe 60s this afternoon. Just before midnight, the dew point at \neven MSP reached 79, which is quite rare. Despite this, heat \nindices will climb back to 100 across southern/east central MN \nand parts of western WI as air temperatures rise quickly this \nmorning. Elevated smoke will return from fires in the Pacific \nNorthwest, which may temper highs a bit, but the hot overnight \nlows expected will give us a decent head start. The drier air\nthis afternoon will also make the air easier to heat, which may\noffset the increased smoke some. \n\nThe trough will largely bypass us to the east early this week.\nWhile we'll knock down the dew points and the intensity of the\nheat some, temperatures are still going to be above normal\nheading into midweek. \n\nA shortwave trough will round the ridge, centered over the\nsouthern Rockies, to the northern Plains Wednesday night and \nthe Upper Midwest Thursday night. There will be a lot of \nmoisture to work with as pwats increase to 2-2.25 inches. Severe\nweather risk appears negligible due to near moist adiabatic \nlapse rates, but showers and embedded thunderstorms have the\npotential to produce heavy rainfall.\n\nTemperatures return to near normal for Friday and the weekend,\nbut there are indications of the heat returning early next week.",
